WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:05.280
Kia Ora, we’re here at Woodend Beach at one of
our emergency warning sirens.

00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:12.460
These sounded the night of the November Kaikoura
earthquake.  There was some confusion around

00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:15.120
what the sirens meant, and who had to evacuate.

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:19.780
Civil Defence is running a series of public
information nights in the coastal communities

00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:21.360
of the Waimakairi District.

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:26.080
This is your opportunity to hear the latest
advice from our experts, to learn more about

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:29.740
how the warning siren system operates and
ask us any questions you may have.

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:32.560
Be prepared for Tsunami emergencies.

00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:36.740
Tell you neighbours, come along and know what
to do for next time.

00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:38.450
All meetings start at 7pm.

00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:43.900
16 March – Woodend Community Centre
22 March – Pegasus Bay School Hall

00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:50.920
27 March – Kaiapoi Rugby Clubrooms
6 April – Pines / Kairaki Yacht Club

